      "text": "Bengali has no word for 'am / is / are' in the simple present when you say what someone or something is. You just put the two words together: আমি ছাত্র (I student) means 'I am a student'. But you do need a verb when you say that somebody or something is in a place or exists. That verb is আছে, a form of থাকা. The forms of আছ- cover the present; the past and the future use ছিল and থাকবে."
