      "t": "p",
      "text": "For feelings, Bengali says the feeling 'comes to' the person. The person takes the possessive form (আমার, তোমার, তার), not the subject form. So 'I am hungry' is আমার খিদে পেয়েছে, literally 'of me hunger has been got'."
